# Environment file for fim-agent.service (D36/RN-130).
#
# install.sh installs this file at /etc/fim-agent/env ONLY IF that path does
# not already exist, with mode 0600 owned by root:root — systemd reads
# EnvironmentFile= as root before dropping privileges, so the service user
# never needs read access to it.
#
# FIM_BOOTSTRAP_SECRET is required only for the agent's FIRST boot on a host
# with no valid certificate yet (see agent/__main__.py, agent/bootstrap.py).
# It is single-use: once bootstrap succeeds the agent holds a certificate and
# never reads this value again. Uncomment, set it, start the service once,
# then remove the line (or delete the file) — the unit declares
# `EnvironmentFile=-/etc/fim-agent/env` (leading dash), so a missing file
# never prevents startup after bootstrap.

#FIM_BOOTSTRAP_SECRET=
